  "pinnedSource": {
    "src/endpoints/stable-diffusion.js:1038": "pollinations generate: GET /image/<encodeURIComponent(prompt)> with a URLSearchParams query in fixed order and a content-type-derived format",
    "src/endpoints/stable-diffusion.js:778": "together generate: POST /v1/images/generations with the pinned body order, then a URL fallback fetch when b64_json is absent"
  },
  "mechanism": "Both upstreams are hardcoded literals, so the probe replaces only the pinned server node-fetch module (and the global fetch) with a controlled peer (tools/lib/pinned-outbound.mjs); the Go side uses the existing sd seams (sdPollinationsURL / sdTogetherURL) and replays the same peer through a real local listener.",
  "fields": [
    {
      "path": "scenarios.*.response.status",
      "comparison": "compared",
      "reason": "the pinned handlers choose 200/400/500 themselves"
    },
    {
      "path": "scenarios.*.response.headers",
      "comparison": "compared",
      "reason": "Express and the pinned middleware stack set them"
    },
    {
      "path": "scenarios.*.response.body",
      "comparison": "compared",
      "reason": "the projection, including the base64 image and the content-type-derived format"
    },
    {
      "path": "scenarios.*.outbound[].url",
      "comparison": "compared",
      "reason": "path encoding and the query order/values are endpoint behaviour; the random seed is normalized"
    },
    {
      "path": "scenarios.*.outbound[].method",
      "comparison": "compared",
      "reason": "pollinations GET versus together POST"
    },
    {
      "path": "scenarios.*.outbound[].body",
      "comparison": "compared",
      "reason": "the together body member order and omitted undefined members"
    },
    {
      "path": "scenarios.*.outbound[].headers",
      "comparison": "shape",
      "reason": "only the declared content-type and authorization headers are asserted"
    },
    {
      "path": "image bytes",
      "comparison": "compared",
      "reason": "the pinned image bytes are synthetic and known; a real provider answer would be `shape` only"
    }
  ],
  "normalizations": [
    "The Pollinations and Together seeds are `Math.floor(Math.random() * 10_000_000)` when the request seed is negative or absent, so they are replaced by <seed> in the recorded URL/body. They are the only nondeterministic values.",
    "Synthetic credentials and synthetic image bytes only."
  ],
